 ## Overview
-Stochastic Ray-Casting Voxelization determines the interior status of voxels by casting multiple random rays from each voxel center and counting intersections with mesh triangles [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [Ray-Cast Style Voxel Filling](1502-ray-cast-style-voxel-filling.md) and [Front/Back Face Flagging](1506-front-back-face-flagging.md) by relying on statistical majority voting over randomized directions rather than deterministic axis-aligned rays or face orientation flags, making it robust against non-manifold geometry, broken meshes, and self-intersections where a single deterministic ray might fail [S1, unofficial].
